<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's Titasz reports lower losses in 1996.</title>
<headline>Hungary's Titasz reports lower losses in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating result		674.1 loss vs   1,297.5 loss</p>
<p>    Pre-tax result		2,165.8 loss vs   2,678.9 loss</p>
<p>    Net sales		    26,590.1	vs  21,308.0</p>
<p>    Other revenue		   434.8	vs     274.6</p>
<p>    Direct costs of sales    25,049.4	vs  20,719.0</p>
<p>    Indirect costs of sales   2,101.6	vs   1,502.1</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	    548.0	vs     659.0</p>
<p>    Net financial income	1,481.2 loss vs   1,378.9 loss</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	    11.2	vs	36.4</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure   1,492.4	vs   1,415.3</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income     10.5 loss vs	 2.6 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Tiszantuli Aramszolgaltato Rt (Titasz) is a regional electricity supplier. The 1996 figures are preliminary, not audited. Titasz is not listed on the Budapest Stock Exchange, but its shares trade on the OTC market. Germany's Isar-Amperwerke AG holds a 49.23 percent stake in it.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
